  "content": "<!--\nrdf:RDF xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\"\n         xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\"\n         xmlns:trackback=\"http://madskills.com/public/xml/rss/module/trackback/\">\n    <rdf:Description\n        rdf:about=\"/abs/2608.19628\"\n        dc:identifier=\"/abs/2608.19628\"\n        dc:title=\"A Thread-Register Decoupled GPU Execution Model for Efficient Tensor Computation\"\n        trackback:ping=\"/trackback/2608.19628\" />\n    </rdf:RDF>\n-->\n<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <div id=\"abs-outer\">\n   <div class=\"leftcolumn\">\n    <div class=\"subheader\">\n     <h1>Computer Science &gt; Hardware Architecture</h1>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"header-breadcrumbs-mobile\">\n     <strong>arXiv:2608.19628</strong> (cs)\n    </div>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/static/base/1.0.1/css/abs.css\">\n    <div id=\"content-inner\">\n     <div id=\"abs\">\n      <div class=\"dateline\">[Submitted on 20 Aug 2026]</div>\n      <div class=\"authors\">\n       <span class=\"descriptor\">Authors:</span><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Liu,+Z\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zihan Liu</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Leng,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jingwen Leng</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhou,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yangjie Zhou</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Ding,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yitong Ding</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhu,+G\" rel=\"nofollow\">Guanlin Zhu</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Huang,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yilu Huang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Jin,+C\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chiheng Jin</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang,+C\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chen Zhang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Sun,+S\" rel=\"nofollow\">Shixuan Sun</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Feng,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yu Feng</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wu,+A\" rel=\"nofollow\">Anbang Wu</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Guo,+M\" rel=\"nofollow\">Minyi Guo</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Weng,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jian Weng</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Tu,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jiajin Tu</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wang,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Junsong Wang</a>\n      </div>\n      <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.19628\">View PDF</a> <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2608.19628v1\">HTML (experimental)</a>\n      <blockquote class=\"abstract mathjax\">\n       <span class=\"descriptor\">Abstract:</span>Modern GPUs increasingly integrate Tensor Cores into the execution pipeline. Although aggregate tensor throughput continues to grow, aided by an operand supply that has evolved from register-based in Ampere to redundancy-free, memory-based in Hopper and Blackwell, efficiently orchestrating the complete tensor compute pipeline for the modern AI workloads remains challenging. We identify the fundamental bottlenecks as fixed parallelism and coarse-grained scheduling, both of which are exposed by modern AI workloads that interleave diverse non-GEMM operations with GEMM. To orchestrate tensor computation efficiently, we propose FIBER, a new architecture that extends the GPU SIMT (single instruction, multiple thread) model. Its basic execution instance, the \\emph{fiber}, is decoupled from private register ownership, carrying only minimal control state while accessing an SM's registers through a shared view. This enables dynamic parallelism scaling, fine-grained register-level dataflow scheduling, and offers a redundancy-free alternative for matrix operand supply. We extend the ISA, microarchitecture, and compiler to realize shared-register addressing, conflict-free operand delivery, and fiber-based program mapping. Under a typical mixed-precision LLM serving scenario, FIBER achieves a 2.25x end-to-end speedup on Ampere (1.15x for the original FP16 computation), with 1.8x and 2.09x on Hopper and Blackwell respectively, and kernel-level gains up to 2.49x.\n      </blockquote>\n      <!--CONTEXT-->\n      <div class=\"metatable\">\n       <table summary=\"Additional metadata\">\n        <tbody>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Subjects:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell subjects\"><span class=\"primary-subject\">Hardware Architecture (cs.AR)</span></td>\n         </tr>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Cite as:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxivid\"><span class=\"arxivid\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.19628\">arXiv:2608.19628</a> [cs.AR]</span></td>\n         </tr>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxividv\">(or <span class=\"arxivid\"> <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.19628v1\">arXiv:2608.19628v1</a> [cs.AR]</span> for this version)</td>\n         </tr>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxivdoi\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.19628\" id=\"arxiv-doi-link\">https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.19628</a>\n           <div class=\"button-and-tooltip\">\n            <button class=\"more-info\" aria-describedby=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n             <svg height=\"15\" role=\"presentation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\">\n              <path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M256 8C119.043 8 8 119.083 8 256c0 136.997 111.043 248 248 248s248-111.003 248-248C504 119.083 392.957 8 256 8zm0 110c23.196 0 42 18.804 42 42s-18.804 42-42 42-42-18.804-42-42 18.804-42 42-42zm56 254c0 6.627-5.373 12-12 12h-88c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-24c0-6.627 5.373-12 12-12h12v-64h-12c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-24c0-6.627 5.373-12 12-12h64c6.627 0 12 5.373 12 12v100h12c6.627 0 12 5.373 12 12v24z\" />\n             </svg>\n             <span class=\"visually-hidden\">Focus to learn more</span>\n            </button>\n            <!-- tooltip description -->\n            <div role=\"tooltip\" id=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n             <span class=\"left-corner\"></span> arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)\n            </div>\n           </div></td>\n         </tr>\n        </tbody>\n       </table>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"submission-history\">\n     <h2>Submission history</h2>\n     From: Zihan Liu [<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/show-email/a51aa1b6/2608.19628\" rel=\"nofollow\">view email</a>]\n     <br>\n     <strong>[v1]</strong> Thu, 20 Aug 2026 04:35:13 UTC (617 KB)\n     <br>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n   <!--end leftcolumn-->\n   <div class=\"extra-services\">\n    <div class=\"full-text\">\n     <a name=\"other\"></a> <span class=\"descriptor\">Full-text links:</span>\n     <h2>Access Paper:</h2>\n     <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.19628\" aria-describedby=\"download-button-info\" accesskey=\"f\" class=\"abs-button download-pdf\">View PDF</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2608.19628v1\" class=\"abs-button\" id=\"latexml-download-link\">HTML (experimental)</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/src/2608.19628\" class=\"abs-button download-eprint\">TeX Source </a></li>\n     </ul>\n     <div class=\"abs-license\">\n      <a href=\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\" title=\"Rights to this article\">view license</a>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <!--end full-text-->\n    <div class=\"browse\">\n     <h3 class=\"browse-context-heading\">Current browse context:</h3>\n     <div class=\"current\">cs.AR</div>\n     <div class=\"prevnext\">\n      <span class=\"arrow\"> <a class=\"abs-button prev-url\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/prevnext?id=2608.19628&amp;function=prev&amp;context=cs.AR\" accesskey=\"p\" title=\"previous in cs.AR (accesskey p)\" rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;&nbsp;prev</a> </span> <span class=\"is-hidden-mobile\">&nbsp; | &nbsp;</span> <span class=\"arrow\"> <a class=\"abs-button next-url\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/prevnext?id=2608.19628&amp;function=next&amp;context=cs.AR\" accesskey=\"n\" title=\"next in cs.AR (accesskey n)\" rel=\"nofollow\">next&nbsp;&gt;</a> </span>\n      <br>\n     </div>\n     <div class=\"list\">\n      <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small context-new\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AR/new\" rel=\"nofollow\">new</a> <span class=\"is-hidden-mobile\"> | </span> <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small context-recent\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AR/recent\" rel=\"nofollow\">recent</a> <span class=\"is-hidden-mobile\"> | </span><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small context-id\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AR/2026-08\" rel=\"nofollow\">2026-08</a>\n     </div>\n     <div class=\"abs-switch-cat\">\n      Change to browse by:\n      <div class=\"switch context-change\">\n       <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.19628?context=cs\" rel=\"nofollow\">cs</a>\n       <br class=\"is-hidden-mobile\">\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"extra-ref-cite\">\n     <h3>References &amp; Citations</h3>\n     <ul>\n      <li><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-small cite-ads\" href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/arXiv:2608.19628\">NASA ADS</a></li>\n      <li><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-small cite-google-scholar\" href=\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?arxiv_id=2608.19628\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Google Scholar</a></li>\n      <li><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-small cite-semantic-scholar\" href=\"https://api.semanticscholar.org/arXiv:2608.19628\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Semantic Scholar</a></li>\n     </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"extra-ref-cite\">\n     <button type=\"button\" id=\"bib-cite-trigger\" class=\"bib-cite-button abs-button\">export BibTeX citation</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bookmarks\">\n     <div>\n      <h3>Bookmark</h3>\n     </div>\n     <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small\" href=\"http://www.bibsonomy.org/BibtexHandler?requTask=upload&amp;url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.19628&amp;description=A Thread-Register Decoupled GPU Execution Model for Efficient Tensor Computation\" title=\"Bookmark on BibSonomy\"> <img src=\"https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/social/bibsonomy.png\" alt=\"BibSonomy\"> </a> <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small\" href=\"https://reddit.com/submit?url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.19628&amp;title=A Thread-Register Decoupled GPU Execution Model for Efficient Tensor Computation\" title=\"Bookmark on Reddit\"> <img src=\"https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/social/reddit.png\" alt=\"Reddit\"> </a>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n   <!--end extra-services-->\n   <!-- LABS AREA -->\n   <div id=\"labstabs\"></div>\n   <!-- END LABS AREA -->\n   <div class=\"endorsers\">\n    <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/auth/show-endorsers/2608.19628\" class=\"endorser-who\" rel=\"nofollow\">Which authors of this paper are endorsers?</a> | Disable MathJax (<a href=\"https://info.arxiv.org/help/mathjax.html\">What is MathJax?</a>) <span class=\"help\" style=\"font-style: normal; float: right; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 1em;\"></span>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "FIBER 引入了一种新颖的 GPU 执行模型，将线程与私有寄存器所有权解耦，从而实现动态并行性和细粒度数据流调度，显著提高张量计算效率。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "FIBER 引入了一种新颖的 GPU 执行模型，将线程与私有寄存器所有权解耦，从而实现动态并行性和细粒度数据流调度，显著提高张量计算效率。",
  "summary": "该论文提出了 FIBER，一种扩展 SIMT 模型的 GPU 架构，通过将执行实例（纤维）与私有寄存器所有权分离，实现了动态并行性扩展、高效的寄存器级数据流调度，以及无冗余的矩阵操作数供应。该模型在 ISA、微架构和编译器层面均有实现，在混合精度 LLM 服务场景中显示出显著的加速效果。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "线程与寄存器的解耦",
      "explanation": "FIBER 将执行实例（纤维）与私有寄存器所有权分离。纤维携带最小的控制状态，并访问 SM 寄存器的共享视图，从而实现更灵活、更高效的资源管理。"
    },
    {
      "point": "动态并行性和调度",
      "explanation": "该架构支持动态并行性扩展和细粒度寄存器级数据流调度。这对于交织多种非 GEMM 操作与 GEMM 的现代 AI 工作负载尤为有利，因为它有助于克服固定并行性和粗粒度调度的限制。"
    },
    {
      "point": "无冗余的操作数供应",
      "explanation": "FIBER 提供了一种无冗余的矩阵操作数供应替代方案。通过共享寄存器，系统可以避免在私有寄存器之间复制数据所带来的开销，从而实现更高效的计算。"
    },
    {
      "point": "显著的性能提升",
      "explanation": "论文报告在 Ampere 上实现了 2.25 倍的端到端加速，在 Hopper 和 Blackwell 架构上也有显著提升。在内核级别，观察到高达 2.49 倍的改进，证明了该模型在实际场景中的有效性。"
    }
  ],
  "keyQuotes": [
    "我们发现根本性的瓶颈是固定并行性和粗粒度调度，这两种问题都被交织了多种非 GEMM 操作与 GEMM 的现代 AI 工作负载所暴露。"
  ],
